  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EULFCompliance">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">DEFINITION:
EULF compliance ABB is a Principle consisting of a package of case studies, specifications, guidelines, training materials, recommendations and actions required by public administrations and stakeholder communities to facilitate the implementation, use and expansion of INSPIRE in an e-government context.

Source: Joinup
(&lt;a href=&quot;https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/news/attachment/jrc103110_1-dc246-d3.2_eulf_guideline_on_location_privacy_v1.00_final_-_pubsy.pdf&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/news/attachment/jrc1031…&lt;/a&gt;)

EXAMPLES:
The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB):</skos:definition>
