  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/SecurityPolicyBusinessObject">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Definition: Security Policy ABB is a Business Object that regulates the protection of customer or client's data.

Source: Gartner

Source reference: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gartner.com/en/information-technology/glossary/security&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://www.gartner.com/en/information-technology/glossary/security&lt;/a&gt;

Example: The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Common Foreign and Security Policy (CFSP) - The Common Foreign and Security Policy (CFSP) is the organised, agreed foreign policy of the European Union (EU) for mainly security and defence diplomacy and actions. &lt;a href=&quot;https://eeas.europa.eu/topics/common-foreign-security-policy-cfsp_en&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://eeas.europa.eu/topics/common-foreign-security-policy-cfsp_en&lt;/a&gt;

IoP Dimension: Governance IoP

LOST view: Semantic view

Interoperability saliency: The Security Policy ABB is salient for semantic interoperability because it provides a guiding framework to ensure the security of data and information according to interoperability principles as stated in the EIF recommendation n° 46 and 47: &quot;Consider the specific security and privacy requirements and identify measures for the provision of each public service according to risk management plans.&quot;

Identifier: &lt;a href=&quot;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/SecurityPolicyBusinessObject&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/SecurityPolicyBusinessObject&lt;/a&gt;

