  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TelemetryTechnologyService">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Definition: Telemetry ABB is a Technology Service that enables the procedures to automatically measure and analyse information about public administration services and IT platforms to track performance and identify issues.

Source: EEA

Source reference: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eea.europa.eu/help/glossary/gemet-environmental-thesaurus/telemetry&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://www.eea.europa.eu/help/glossary/gemet-environmental-thesaurus/t…&lt;/a&gt;

Example: The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Telemetry is a clear example of use in computers integrated in spacecrafts. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.esa.int/Enabling_Support/Space_Engineering_Technology/Onboard_Computers_and_Data_Handling/Telemetry_Telecommand&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://www.esa.int/Enabling_Support/Space_Engineering_Technology/Onboa…&lt;/a&gt;

LOST view: Technical view - Infrastructure

Interoperability saliency: Telemetry is salient for semantic and technical interoperability because it sets up the mechanisms to monitor a specific ICT system to (i) collect behavioural information, and (ii) understand the ICT system's behaviour during its execution.

Identifier: &lt;a href=&quot;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TelemetryTechnologyService&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TelemetryTechnologyService&lt;/a&gt;

