  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TransationEnablersGrouping">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Definition: Machine Translation Enablers ABB is a Groping that refers to tools or components that facilitate the translation of text from one language to another using machine learning techniques

Source: Inspired in eTranslation

Source reference: &lt;a href=&quot;https://commission.europa.eu/resources-partners/etranslation_en&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://commission.europa.eu/resources-partners/etranslation_en&lt;/a&gt;

IoP Dimension: Structural IoP, Behavioral IoP

LOST view: Technical view - application

Interoperability saliency: The Translation Enablers Grouping ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it comprises a set of tools and components that ensure the translation of digital public services to different languages in the European Union by using machine learning techniques.

Identifier: &lt;a href=&quot;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TransationEnablersGrouping&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TransationEnablersGrouping&lt;/a&gt;

