  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EdgeComputingTechnologyCollaboration_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-31</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Edge Computing ABB is a Technology Collaboration that enables the procedures to implement a distributed computing topology where information processing is located close to the edge, where things and people produce or consume that information</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Edge Computing</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Edge Computing</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:EdgeComputingTechnologyCollaboration</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): SovereignEDGE.eu https://sovereignedge.eu/</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EdgeComputingTechnologyCollaboration</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>Gartner</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Edge Computing ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it provides needed computational elements and tools to perform data analytics in specific devices that can nurture public administration digital services (e.g. mobiles from citizens).</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EdgeComputingTechnologyCollaboration"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.gartner.com/en/information-technology/glossary/edge-computing</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EdgeComputingTechnologyCollaboration</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EdgeComputingTechnologyCollaboration_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifInteroperabilityLevelBusinessObject_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-23</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>EIF Interoperability Level ABB is a Business Object setting guidelines for developing public services. The EIF defines four interoperability levels, which cover legal, organisational, semantic and technical interoperability. Each level deserves special attention when a new European public service is established.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of EIF Interoperability Level</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of EIF Interoperability Level</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:EifInteroperabilityLevelBusinessObject</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): The EIF defines four interoperability levels, which cover legal, organisational, semantic and technical interoperability.</skos:example>
    <eira:definitionSource>European Commission, ISA Programme. The New European Interoperability Framework (EIF) for European public services. [Online] 2017</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifInteroperabilityLevelBusinessObject</eira:PURI>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Governance IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency></eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:viewpoint>EIRA Ontology viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifInteroperabilityLevelBusinessObject"/>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>(https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/eif_en.)</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifInteroperabilityLevelBusinessObject</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifInteroperabilityLevelBusinessObject_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifPrinciple_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-23</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>EIF Principle ABB is a Principle analysing European Public Services by driving the identification and formulation of interoperability requirements with higher levels of granularity and used to design European public services by driving the identification and formulation of interoperability specifications</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of EIF Principle</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of EIF Principle</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:EifPrinciple</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Transparency: EIF Transparency Principle refers to: 1. Enabling visibility inside the administrative environment of a public administration. This is about allowing other public administrations, citizens and businesses to view and understand administrative rules, processes, data, services and decision-making.  2. Ensuring availability of interfaces with internal information systems. Public administrations operate a large number of what are often heterogeneous and disparate information systems in support of their internal processes. Interoperability depends on ensuring the availability of interfaces to these systems and the data they handle. In turn, interoperability facilitates reuse of systems and data, and enables these to be integrated into larger systems. 3. Securing the right to the protection of personal data, by respecting the applicable legal framework for the large volumes of personal data of citizens, held and managed by Public administrations.(https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/default/files/eif_brochure_final.pdf)</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>EIF</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifPrinciple</eira:PURI>
    <eira:iopSaliency></eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:viewpoint>Interoperability Privacy viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:viewpoint>Key Interoperability Enablers viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:viewpoint>Interoperability Security viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:viewpoint>EIRA Ontology viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifPrinciple"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifPrinciple_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifPrinciple</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/eif_en</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EiraArchitectureBuildingBlock_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of EIRA Architecture Building Block</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of EIRA Architecture Building Block</skos:prefLabel>
