  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ExternalFacility_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>External Facility ABB is a Facility that enables a physical location or infrastructure that is owned or operated by a third-party organization and used by another organization or individual. These facilities may include office buildings, data centres, warehouses, manufacture</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of External Facility</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of External Facility</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:ExternalFacility</dc:type>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ExternalFacility</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>ISA2-EIA</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The External Facility ABB is saliency for organizational and technical interoperability because it establishes the business rules and responsibilities to share infrastructures for the use of public administrations. The ABB also provides the application of open specifications and solutions to make interoperable public administration solutions.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ExternalFacility"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ExternalFacility_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ExternalFacility</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/actions/towards-european-interoperability-architecture_en/</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ExternalTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>External Service ABB is a Technology Service that enables the procedures to offer services that are delivered by a third-party organization or vendor.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of External Service</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of External Service</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:ExternalTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ExternalTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in Gartner</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The External Service ABB is salient for organizational and semantic interoperability because it establishes the business rules and responsibilities to share digital services on the use of the public administration to complement the existing ones. This ABB also provides standardised data exchange models to share the information provided by external services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ExternalTechnologyService"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ExternalTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ExternalTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.gartner.com/en/information-technology/glossary/esp-external-services-provider</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/FacilityLocation_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Facility Location ABB is a Location conceptual or physical place or position where a bussiness organization is placed.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Facility Location</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Facility Location</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:FacilityLocation</dc:type>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/FacilityLocation</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in Archimate</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Facility Location ABB is salient for the organizational and technical interoperability because of (i) it determines the interlink between public administration business process removing existing barriers; (ii) set up needed mechanism between IT systems to remove fragmentation in service delivery.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/FacilityLocation"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/FacilityLocation_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/FacilityLocation</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://pubs.opengroup.org/architecture/archimate3-doc/chap04.html</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/FederatedIdentityProviderTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Federated Identity Provider ABB is a Technology Service that enables users to access multiple applications and services across different organizations or domains using a single set of credentials</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Federated Identity Provider</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Federated Identity Provider</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:FederatedIdentityProviderTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Federated Identity can be achieved by implementing the OpenID Connect Federation specification.  https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-federation-1_0.html</skos:example>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inpired in eIDAS</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/FederatedIdentityProviderTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Federated Identity Provider ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it conforms to the network of identity provider systems to distribute the transference and identification of stakeholders to access and make use of public services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/FederatedIdentityProviderTechnologyService"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/FederatedIdentityProviderTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/FederatedIdentityProviderTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidas-regulation</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/FileStorageTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>File storage ABB is a Technology Service that implements the behaviour of a software tool that refers to the process of storing and organizing digital files in a secure and efficient manner</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of File Storage</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of File Storage</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:FileStorageTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): GARTNER- Distributed File Systems and Objects Storage Reviews and Ratings. https://www.gartner.com/reviews/market/distributed-file-systems-and-object-storage</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/FileStorageTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in the definition provided by relebant database vendors</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>File Storage ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it set up the data integration mechanism based on different files. This kind of file storage permit also ensures data provenance of the information considering file modification and creation.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/FileStorageTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference></eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/FileStorageTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/FileStorageTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

