  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeDiscoveryApplicationComponent_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-20</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Knowledge Discovery ABB is an Application Component that enables the implementation of processes where a lot of data manipulation tools with different characteristics have to be used together to reach the goal of previously unknown, potentially useful information extraction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Knowledge Discovery</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Knowledge Discovery</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:KnowledgeDiscoveryApplicationComponent</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): CELLAR. Cellar metadata is stored in a knowledge graph, and more specifically in a triple store. A SPARQL interface is used to query the metadata. https://op.europa.eu/en/web/cellar/cellar-data/metadata/knowledge-graph</skos:example>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in EUROSTAT</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeDiscoveryApplicationComponent</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Knowledge Discovery Application Component ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it contributes to performing a highly complex process where a lot of data manipulation tools with different characteristics have to be used together to reach the goal of previously unknown, potentially useful information extraction.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeDiscoveryApplicationComponent"/>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Glossary:Knowledge-intensive_services_(KIS)</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeDiscoveryApplicationComponent</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeDiscoveryApplicationComponent_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeDiscoveryApplicationService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-20</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Knowledge Discovery ABB is an Application Service that enables a highly complex process where a lot of data manipulation tools with different characteristics have to be used together to reach the goal of previously unknown, potentially useful information extraction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Knowledge Discovery</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Knowledge Discovery</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:KnowledgeDiscoveryApplicationService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): CELLAR. Cellar metadata is stored in a knowledge graph, and more specifically in a triple store. A SPARQL interface is used to query the metadata. https://op.europa.eu/en/web/cellar/cellar-data/metadata/knowledge-graph</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeDiscoveryApplicationService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in EUROSTAT</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Knowledge Discovery Application Service ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it performs a series of complex processes that incorporate multiple data channels, formats and characteristics that are processed to extract relevant information to be used by other digital public services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeDiscoveryApplicationService"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeDiscoveryApplicationService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeDiscoveryApplicationService</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Glossary:Knowledge-intensive_services_(KIS)</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeDiscoveryEnablers_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Knowledge discovery Enablers ABB is a Grouping that refers to components and services that facilitate the process of discovering insights and knowledge from data</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Knowledge Discovery Enablers</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Knowledge Discovery Enablers</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:KnowledgeDiscoveryEnablers</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): CELLAR. Cellar metadata is stored in a knowledge graph, and more specifically in a triple store. A SPARQL interface is used to query the metadata. https://op.europa.eu/en/web/cellar/cellar-data/metadata/knowledge-graph</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>European Comission-Open Science</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeDiscoveryEnablers</eira:PURI>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Knowledge Discovery Enablers Grouping ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it comprises tools, data services and components that enable and enhance the knowledge discovery process from data and information.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeDiscoveryEnablers"/>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://research-and-innovation.ec.europa.eu/strategy/strategy-2020-2024/our-digital-future/open-science_en</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeDiscoveryEnablers</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeDiscoveryEnablers_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeRepresentation_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Knowledge ABB is a Representation that refers to a perceptible form of stored information in a human/artificial memory representing the understanding and awareness that a person has about a particular subject, topic, or area of study. Knowledge is generally context related.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Knowledge</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Knowledge</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:KnowledgeRepresentation</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Core Vocabularies for public administration. https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre/core-vocabularies</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeRepresentation</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>FREE DICTIONARY</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency></eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:viewpoint>Highlevel viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:view>Semantic view</eira:view>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeRepresentation"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeRepresentation</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeRepresentation_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://encyclopedia2.thefreedictionary.com/knowledge</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeTriplestore_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-20</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Knowledge Triplestore ABB is a Data Object that enables storage, management and retrieval of data in the form of triples, data entities composed of subject-predicate-object.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Knowledge Triplestore</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Knowledge Triplestore</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:KnowledgeTriplestore</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): CELLAR. Cellar metadata is stored in a knowledge graph, and more specifically in a triple store. A SPARQL interface is used to query the metadata. https://op.europa.eu/en/web/cellar/cellar-data/metadata/knowledge-graph</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeTriplestore</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>W3C</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Knowledge Triplestore Data Object ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it represents the different data objects such as databases storing data, allowing to manage and retrieve of data from different sources and digital public services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeTriplestore"/>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.w3.org/2001/sw/Europe/events/20031113-storage/positions/rusher.html</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeTriplestore_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/KnowledgeTriplestore</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalActRepresentation_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-12-1</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Legal Act Representation ABB is a Representation manifesting the content of a legal Act in a digital format, thus making possible digital public services to exchange such content.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Legal Act Representation</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Legal Act Representation</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:LegalActRepresentation</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): The XML specification Akoma Ntoso is used  to address the need of the public administration and European Institutions to generate draft legislation in the legal XML format Akoma Ntoso (the OASIS TC LegalXMLDocument). This specification is used by LEOS (Legislation Editing Open Software, https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/justice-law-and-security/solution/leos-open-source-software-editing-legislation/release/330).</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalActRepresentation</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>Based on the IFLA concepts of 'manifestation' and Legal Act.</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Legal Act Representation ABB is salient for the Behavioural Interoperability because it enables the exchange, reading and processing of Legal Acts. It is also salient for the Structural Interoperability since the content digitally represented can be searched and reused in different domains and for differnt purposes.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:modelType>Behavioural IoP, Structural IoP</eira:modelType>
    <eira:viewpoint>Highlevel viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:view>Legal view</eira:view>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalActRepresentation"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalActRepresentation_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalActRepresentation</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://repository.ifla.org/handle/123456789/40</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note>Legal Act Representation can be human or machine readable. In the context of digital public services they are, either way, digitally supported (i.e., no physical sypports like paper or other that are not bytes are involved in the exchange of data and information).</skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalActRequirement_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-09-1</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Legal Act ABB is a Business Object formalising a set of rules on a subject potentially including requirements concerning digital public services.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Legal Act</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Legal Act</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:LegalActRequirement</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): The COMMISSION REGULATION (EU) 2018/1881 of 3 December 2018 amending Regulation (EC) No 1907/2006 of the European Parliament and of the Council on the Registration, Evaluation, Authorisation and Restriction of Chemicals (REACH) as regards Annexes I, III,VI, VII, VIII, IX, X, XI, and XII to address nanoforms of substances (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?qid=1544102387245&amp;uri=CELEX:32018R1881) is an example of an SBB implementing a Legal Act ABB.</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalActRequirement</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>European Union Law</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Governance IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Legal Act ABB is salient for legal interoperability because it helps establish legal rules by ensuring compatible legal/juridical certainty in the exchange of information.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:viewpoint>Highlevel viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:viewpoint>Interoperability Privacy viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:synonym>Legal Instrument</eira:synonym>
    <eira:view>Legal view</eira:view>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalActRequirement"/>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://eur-lex.europa.eu/summary/glossary/legislative_acts.html</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalActRequirement</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalActRequirement_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note>The granularity of the requirements might be of high level or detail level. Requirements of high-level granularity contain generic/abstract functional requirements like principles and/or recommendations with considerable degrees for transposition/execution and of not binding nature. On the other side, requirements of detail-level granularity imply a limited degree for transposition/execution and they contain specific/concrete functionalities, solution components, data, procedures, and/or technical specifications or standards to be used. EU legal acts are legislative or non-legislative acts adopted by the European institutions (Article 288 TFEU). With the entry into force of the Treaty of Lisbon on 1 December 2009. The names &quot;European Union&quot; or &quot;EU&quot; have replaced &quot;European Community&quot;, &quot;Community&quot; or &quot;EC&quot;.</skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalAgreementContract_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-10-1</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Legal Agreement ABB is a Contract enabling collaboration between digital public services cross legal jurisdictions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Legal Agreement</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Legal Agreement</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:LegalAgreementContract</dc:type>
    <skos:example>An example of a treaty that does have provisions for further binding agreements is the UN Charter. By signing and ratifying the Charter, countries agreed to be legally bound by resolutions passed by UN bodies such as the General Assembly and the Security Council. Thus, UN resolutions are legally binding on UN Member States, and no signature or ratification is necessary. https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=2ahUKEwiA3djvvbT2AhX1SPEDHdmuCqMQFnoECAYQAQ&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.phe.gov%2Fs3%2Flaw%2FPages%2FInternational.aspx&amp;usg=AOvVaw23fJMEr0G7JOPyleNl2lrd</skos:example>
    <eira:definitionSource>EIF</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalAgreementContract</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Governance IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Legal Agreement ABB is salient for the governance interoperability because it sets the foundations for the coordination or harmonization between different legislations. Also this ABB is salient for the legal governance in the way of establishing the required business rules facilitate data exchange between public services at lower level.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:viewpoint>Interoperability Governance viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:view>Legal view</eira:view>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalAgreementContract"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalAgreementContract_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalAgreementContract</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=celex%3A12016E207</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note>Generally speaking a Legal Agreement Contract t is of a generic not binding nature like the declarations of Tallinn and Berlin (typically involving many legal jurisdictions). Legal agreements of binding nature typically take the form of binding legal acts like the reference list of offences punishable in the European arrest warrant (2002/584/JHA: Council Framework Decision of 13 June 2002).</skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalAgreements-InternationalTreaties_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Legal Agreement - International Treaties</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Legal Agreement - International Treaties</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:LegalAgreements-InternationalTreaties</dc:type>
    <eira:ABB_Status>Obsolete</eira:ABB_Status>
    <eira:ID>ABB368</eira:ID>
    <owl:deprecated>true</owl:deprecated>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalAgreements-InternationalTreaties"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalAgreements-InternationalTreaties_Properties</dc:identifier>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalClausesRequirement_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-18</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Legal clauses ABB is a Requirement that refers to specific points or topics that permit to specify a legal document.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Legal Clauses</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Legal Clauses</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:LegalClausesRequirement</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Clause 6 - Description of the transfer(s): The details of the transfer(s), and in particular the categories of personal data that are transferred and the purpose(s) for which they are transferred, are specified in Annex I.B. (http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2021/914/oj)</skos:example>
    <eira:definitionSource>European Comision</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalClausesRequirement</eira:PURI>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Governance IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency></eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:view>Legal view</eira:view>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalClausesRequirement"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalClausesRequirement_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalClausesRequirement</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/types-eu-law_en</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalEntityStakeholder_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-12-1</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Legal Entity ABB is a Stakeholder that is a self-empoyed person, company, or organization that has legal rights and obligations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Legal Entity</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Legal Entity</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:LegalEntityStakeholder</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Any instance of Business, Public Administration with legal personality or a Natural person. https://commission.europa.eu/publications/legal-entities_en</skos:example>
    <eira:definitionSource>SEMIC-CBV</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalEntityStakeholder</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Legal Entity ABB is salient for organizational and behavioural interoperability because it permits the identification of procedures and business rules related to this stakeholder that facilitates the exchange of data, information and knowledge between digital public services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalEntityStakeholder"/>
    <eira:view>Organisational view</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalEntityStakeholder_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalEntityStakeholder</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://semiceu.github.io/Core-Business-Vocabulary/releases/2.00/#Legal%20Entity</eira:definitionSourceReference>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalInteroperabilityAgreementContract_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-10-1</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Legal Interoperability Agreement ABB is a Contract formalizing governance rules enabling collaboration between digital public services.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Legal Interoperability Agreement</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Legal Interoperability Agreement</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:LegalInteroperabilityAgreementContract</dc:type>
    <skos:example>RDA-CODATA - Agreement that provides the guidelines and principles on the legal interoperability of research data. (http://www.codata.org/uploads/Legal%20Interoperability%20Principles%20and%20Implementation%20Guidelines_Final2.pdf)</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>EIF</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalInteroperabilityAgreementContract</eira:PURI>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Governance IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Legal Interoperability Agreement ABB is a key interoperability enabler (*) for governance, organizational and legal interoperability by (i) foundations and requirements that enable the seamless exchange of data, information, and knowledge; and (ii) agreement on digital business capabilities that can map locally aligned processes between public administrations.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:viewpoint>Interoperability Security viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:viewpoint>Key Interoperability Enablers viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:viewpoint>Interoperability Governance viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalInteroperabilityAgreementContract"/>
    <eira:view>Legal view</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalInteroperabilityAgreementContract</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalInteroperabilityAgreementContract_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/isa/files/eif_brochure_final.pdf#page=27</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note>The legal Interoperability Agreement ABB is a specialisation of the Legal Agreement. It aims to coordinate or harmonize efficient exchange models between digital public services within a Public Administration and/or cross Public Administrations.</skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalInteroperabilityRequirement_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Legal Interoperability Requirement</skos:notation>
