    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LifecycleManagementService"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LifecycleManagementService_Properties</dc:identifier>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LightweightDirectoryAccessTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Lightweight Directory Access ABB is a Technology Service that enables compliance with an open, vendor-neutral, industry-standard application protocol for accessing and maintaining distributed directory information services over an Internet Protocol (IP) network.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Lightweight Directory Access Protocol</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Lightweight Directory Access Protocol</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:LightweightDirectoryAccessTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Lightweight Directory Access Protocol can be implemented in multiple platforms or systems, allowing to integrating an organisatio'n LDAP-enabled identity management service to other platforms such as Drupal. https://www.drupal.org/docs/contributed-modules/lightweight-directory-access-protocol-ldap</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>CAMSS</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LightweightDirectoryAccessTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Lightweight Directory Access ABB is salient for technical and semantic interoperability because it provides the needed software mechanism and the LDAP data exchange model to manage user authentication, user provisioning and access to public services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LightweightDirectoryAccessTechnologyService"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LightweightDirectoryAccessTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LightweightDirectoryAccessTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LinkedDataEventStreamRepresentation_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-26</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Linked Data Event Stream ABB is a Representation of immutable objects that can be publish, consumed and processing in real-time according to the Linked Data principles.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Linked Data Event Stream</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Linked Data Event Stream</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:LinkedDataEventStreamRepresentation</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): LDES - SEMIC Linked Event Streams pilot for the ERA (European Railway Agency). LDES provides a data publishing alternative based on Linked Data principles, that models dataset changes as a stream of events. This enables opportune data synchronization tasks and access to previous versions of dataset (historic data). In this pilot we aim to establish the foundations and show the benefits of the LDES approach, to power a specific use case required by ERA, namely the infrastructure change alert. https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semantic-interoperability-community-semic/event/semic-linked-data-event-streams-pilot-era-9th-june</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LinkedDataEventStreamRepresentation</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>SEMIC</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Linked Data Event Stream Representation ABB is salient for semantic interoperability because it contributes to secure data consumption and processing ensuring that exchanged data is not modified or altered. The fact of being immutable is relevant to ensure data integrity over time.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LinkedDataEventStreamRepresentation"/>
    <eira:view>Semantic view</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LinkedDataEventStreamRepresentation_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LinkedDataEventStreamRepresentation</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/semic-support-centre</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LinkedDataRepresentation_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-26</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Linked data ABB is a Representation that enables a set of principles and technologies for publishing, sharing, and connecting structured data on the web.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Linked Data</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Linked Data</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:LinkedDataRepresentation</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Publications Office Linked Data Repository. https://op.europa.eu/en/linked-data</skos:example>
    <eira:definitionSource>W3C-Linked Data</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LinkedDataRepresentation</eira:PURI>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Linked Data Representation ABB is salient for semantic interoperability because it provides a set of publishing, sharing, and connection methods that allow linking the data from digital public services, making it more meaningful and increasing the quality and scope of data and services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LinkedDataRepresentation"/>
    <eira:view>Semantic view</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LinkedDataRepresentation</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LinkedDataRepresentation_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.w3.org/standards/semanticweb/data</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LinkedOpenDataRepresentation_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-26</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Linked Open Data ABB is a Representation that enables the procedures of publishing structured data enriched with metadata to ensure data understanding, connection, findability and link with informational resources.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Linked Open Data</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Linked Open Data</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:LinkedOpenDataRepresentation</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): EuropeanaPro https://pro.europeana.eu/page/linked-open-data</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>EUROPEANA PRO</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LinkedOpenDataRepresentation</eira:PURI>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Linked Open Data Representation ABB is salient for semantic interoperability because it provides a set of publishing, sharing, and connection methods that allow linking and publishing the data from digital public services, making it more meaningful and increasing the quality and scope of data and services. Moreover, it increases data discoverability and maximises the reuse and exchange of data.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LinkedOpenDataRepresentation"/>
    <eira:view>Semantic view</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LinkedOpenDataRepresentation_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LinkedOpenDataRepresentation</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://pro.europeana.eu/page/linked-open-data</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LoadBalancerTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Load Balancer ABB is a Technology Service that enables the implementation of a component that distributes incoming network traffic across multiple servers or network resources</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Load Balancer</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Load Balancer</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:LoadBalancerTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): DIGIT/C Hosting Service - DIGIT/C offers a high availability and high performance hosting infrastructure that is being comprised, among other elements, of back-end web server instances and application servers for hosting and serving both static and dynamic sites. http://ec.europa.eu/ipg/build/infrastructure/index_en.htm</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LoadBalancerTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in referent cloud service providers definitions</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Load Balancer ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it provides the functionalities to maintain the traffic to the public administration digital services accordingly with a load that can permit their correct performance.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LoadBalancerTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LoadBalancerTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LoadBalancerTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference></eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LocalAreaCommunicationNetwork_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-31</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Local Area Network ABB is a Communication Network that enables the connection of devices and computers within a limited area.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Local Area Network</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Local Area Network</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:LocalAreaCommunicationNetwork</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): European Commission. https://ec.europa.eu/commission/presscorner/detail/en/MEMO_05_256</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LocalAreaCommunicationNetwork</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>Networkbits</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Local Area Network ABB is salient for technical interoperability as the infrastructure that can connect devices and tools within a limited area of the public administration.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LocalAreaCommunicationNetwork"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://web.archive.org/web/20201026082752/http://networkbits.net/lan-components/local-area-network-lan-basic-components/</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LocalAreaCommunicationNetwork</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LocalAreaCommunicationNetwork_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LoggerTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Logger ABB is a Technology Service that enables the procedures recording events or messages that occur within a system or application</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Logger</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Logger</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:LoggerTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): OECD-OPSI- Quality of Public Administrations - A toolbox for practicioners. https://oecd-opsi.org/toolkits/quality-of-public-administration-a-toolbox-for-practitioners/</skos:example>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in Gartner</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LoggerTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Logger ABB is salient for semantic and technical interoperability due to it defines the mechanisms to manage messages from the applications to enhance their behavioural understanding in the execution or when unexpected behaviours occur. These mechanisms are based on open specifications for messaging representation and exchange.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LoggerTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LoggerTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LoggerTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.gartner.com/en/information-technology/glossary/event-fault-and-log-management</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LoggingComponent_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Logging Component</skos:notation>
