  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/NoSQLDatabaseManagerTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>NoSQL Database Manager ABB is a Technology Service that enables the behaviour of a system that provides access to non-relational databases.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of NoSQL Database Manager</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of NoSQL Database Manager</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:NoSQLDatabaseManagerTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): NoSQL Manager by mongodb. User friendly interface and Shell power. Intuitive interface and high performance of the desktop application save time for beginners and professional database  developers and administrators. https://www.mongodbmanager.com/</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/NoSQLDatabaseManagerTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in the definition provided by relebant noSQL vendors</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>NoSQL Database Manager ABB is salient for semantic interoperability due to its implements mechanism to manipulate NoSQL databases and share data using common data exchange models (e.g. JSON)</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/NoSQLDatabaseManagerTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/NoSQLDatabaseManagerTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/NoSQLDatabaseManagerTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference></eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Non-bindingInstrumentRequirement_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-10-1</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Non-binding Instrument ABB is a Business Object, involving no obligation, which are available to the European institutions to carry out their tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Non-binding Instrument</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Non-binding Instrument</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:Non-bindingInstrumentRequirement</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Opinion of the European Economic and Social Committee on Next Generation SME Strategy — Enhancing Effective and Swift Delivery (own-initiative opinion). https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX%3A52021IE3668&amp;qid=1664779252884</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Non-bindingInstrumentRequirement</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>EUR-Lex</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Governance IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Non-binding Instrument ABB is a key salient for the legal and governance interoperability enabler as a specialisation of the Legal Act, it makes the recommendation of implementation of the policies and rules.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:view>Legal view</eira:view>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Non-bindingInstrumentRequirement"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Non-bindingInstrumentRequirement_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Non-bindingInstrumentRequirement</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>http://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/data/data-validation</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Object-OrientedDatabaseManagerTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Object Oriented Database Manager ABB is a Technology Service that implements the behaviour of a software system that applies concepts of object-oriented programming, and applies them to the management of persistent objects on behalf of multiple users, with capabilities for security, integrity, recovery and contention management</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Object-Oriented Database Manager</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Object-Oriented Database Manager</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:Object-OrientedDatabaseManagerTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): PostgreSQL is an open source object-relational database system that has an edge over other relational databases as the software supports user-defined objects and their behaviors including operators, data types, domains, and indexes. This makes the database software more flexible and robust. https://www.postgresql.org/</skos:example>
    <eira:definitionSource>Gartner</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Object-OrientedDatabaseManagerTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Object Oriented DatabaseManager ABB is salient for semantic interoperability because it implements data management using object-oriented specifications and their corresponding data representation to share the information with different public administration services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Object-OrientedDatabaseManagerTechnologyService"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Object-OrientedDatabaseManagerTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Object-OrientedDatabaseManagerTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.gartner.com/en/information-technology/glossary/oodbms-object-oriented-database-management-system</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/OnPremiseFacility_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-31</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>On Premise Facility ABB is a Facility referring to to a physical location, such as an office or data center, that is owned and managed by a business or organization</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of On Premise Facility</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of On Premise Facility</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:OnPremiseFacility</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): JRC- Development of the EU Green Public Procurement (GPP)- Critaria for Data Centres, Server Rooms and Cloud Services. https://ec.europa.eu/environment/gpp/pdf/jrc118558_2020_0605_data_centres_technical_report_jrc_clean_with_id.pdf</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/OnPremiseFacility</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in The Free Dictionary</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The On Premise Facility ABB is salient for organizational interoperability because it establishes the business rules and responsibilities to place the public administration ICT infrastructure in a custom location.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:viewpoint>Interoperability Security viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/OnPremiseFacility"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/OnPremiseFacility</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/OnPremiseFacility_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://encyclopedia2.thefreedictionary.com/Facility</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/OnceOnly_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Once Only</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Once Only</skos:prefLabel>
